<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        ADDED 2026-08-25 (native LOI/PSA Details). The disposition twin of
        Opportunity.Primary_LOI__c and the sibling of Disposition__c.Primary_NDA__c, whose
        file this one copies. THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY - a
        comment above &lt;CustomField&gt; breaks `sf` at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        🔴 DELETED 2026-08-25, RESTORED 2026-08-26 ON THE USER'S DECISION (option A). The file
        below this comment is the 2026-08-25 original, restored verbatim; the comment is not,
        because HALF OF WHAT IT ARGUED IS NOW WRONG. Read the amendments before trusting a
        sentence in it.

        🔴 THIS FIELD IS WHAT MAKES THE NATIVE LOI DETAILS SECTION POSSIBLE AT ALL - STILL TRUE,
        FOR A DIFFERENT REASON. The retracted original said: "A FlexiPage fieldInstance cannot
        traverse a relationship, but a FORMULA field can - so the five LOI_*__c formula fields in
        this folder read through this lookup and the FlexiPage names them as ordinary Record.
        fields." THE PREMISE IS FALSE: a FlexiPage fieldItem CAN traverse a relationship - it
        names `Record.Primary_LOI__r.Stage__c` directly - which is why the 2026-08-26 rebuild
        needs no mirror fields at all.
        ⚠ SO THE NINE LOI_*__c / PSA_*__c FORMULA MIRRORS AND THE FIVE NDA_*__c ONES STAY DELETED
        AND MUST NOT BE RE-CREATED. They were a workaround for a limitation that does not exist.
        The lookup is the WHOLE dependency now: the section spans it, and a null stamp renders a
        BLANK section exactly as before.

        ⚠ IT RETRACTS A CLAIM THIS REPO MADE IN WRITING ON 2026-08-25, EARLIER THE SAME DAY.
        Disposition_Record_Page.flexipage-meta.xml and DispositionStageEntryService.cls both
        argued, verbatim, "THERE IS NO Primary_LOI__c AND NO Primary_PSA__c on Disposition__c -
        verified against objects/Disposition__c/fields/". That was true when written, became
        false, became true again for one day when this field was deleted, and is false again.
        Every place that reasoned FROM it has been rewritten in the same change, not left to be
        rediscovered.

        THE STAMP IS LOAD-BEARING, NOT BOOKKEEPING, exactly as on Primary_NDA__c.
        DispositionStageEntryService's LOI block writes this through
        DispositionPrimaryChildStampQueueable when it auto-creates the disposition LOI. A row
        whose stamp is missing renders a BLANK Details section - not an error, which is the
        failure shape this repo keeps paying for.
        ⚠ THE BACKFILL MOVED ON 2026-08-26. Rows created before this field existed - now including
        every row created during the 2026-08-25 to 2026-08-26 window when the field did not exist
        at all - are covered by scripts/backfill-disposition-primary-children.apex, an idempotent
        executeAnonymous script. It replaces the `sf data update record` procedure in
        manifest/native-loi-psa/, which is superseded.

        relationshipName is PrimaryDispositions, matching Primary_NDA__c's choice for the same
        reason: LOI__c already carries PrimaryOpportunities (Opportunity.Primary_LOI__c) and
        LOIs (LOI__c.Disposition__c), and a child relationship name must be unique per object.

        deleteConstraint is SetNull, matching both twins: deleting an LOI must clear the
        pointer, never cascade into the disposition.

        🔴 FLS DIVERGES FROM Primary_NDA__c ON PURPOSE, AND THE REASON IS THE BACKFILL - WHICH
        STILL HOLDS, THOUGH THE BACKFILL ITSELF IS A DIFFERENT ARTEFACT NOW. Primary_NDA__c is
        read-only in every set because its trigger is its only writer. This field has a SECOND
        writer: as of 2026-08-26 that is scripts/backfill-disposition-primary-children.apex,
        replacing the `sf data update record` procedure in manifest/native-loi-psa/.
        🔴 ANONYMOUS APEX CANNOT USE SYSTEM_MODE - both `WITH SYSTEM_MODE` and
        `AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE` are rejected with "Cannot use SYSTEM_MODE access level in
        anonymous execution of Apex" (measured on this org 2026-08-24). So the backfill's DML is
        PLAIN, FLS applies to it, and the runner must hold DPEG_Disposition_Edit for it to write
        anything. THE EDIT GRANT IS THEREFORE STILL LOAD-BEARING, not vestigial - and the second
        half of the reason (a user hand-linking a second-round LOI that no automation created)
        stands as well. DPEG_Disposition_View stays read-only.
        ⚠ DO NOT "HARMONISE" THIS TO Primary_NDA__c'S READ-ONLY SHAPE while a backfill is still
        pending - that would silently disarm the script rather than fail it, since a refused
        Database.update with allOrNone = false reports per row and commits the rest.
        (The last clause of the original paragraph - "a formula field cannot carry editable =
        true, which is why the nine LOI_*/PSA_* formulas beside it are read-only in both" - is
        moot: those formulas are deleted and are not coming back.)
    -->
    <fullName>Primary_LOI__c</fullName>
    <deleteConstraint>SetNull</deleteConstraint>
    <description>The primary LOI for this disposition - stamped by the LOI stage-entry automation and spanned by the LOI Details section on the record page (Record.Primary_LOI__r.*). The LOI_*__c formula mirrors this once fed were deleted 2026-08-25 and are not coming back.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Set automatically when the disposition LOI is created. It points the LOI Details section at the right LOI, so it is not maintained by hand.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Primary LOI</label>
    <referenceTo>LOI__c</referenceTo>
    <relationshipLabel>Dispositions (Primary LOI)</relationshipLabel>
    <relationshipName>PrimaryDispositions</relationshipName>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Lookup</type>
</CustomField>
